    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d344">

                <pb facs="0334" n="322" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg322"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.74/14: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Earle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sofia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-18T10:00:00+02:00">July 18, 1941—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>317. The entire Bulgarian press controlled and censored by the Government is
                    rabidly pro-German. In spite of increasingly bitter articles against our country
                    there is as yet no visible evidence of ill will toward America on the part of
                    the people. There remains still a strong memory of all the good deeds of America
                    and Americans for Bulgaria.</p>
                <p>However, with a steady increase in the number and intensity of these press
                    attacks on us an effect on the people must ultimately occur.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
